                <pb facs="0672" n="662" xml:id="pg662"/>

                <head>Appendix D to HD–28</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation<anchor n="8" xml:id="d33-f1"
                    />]</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">supreme economic council</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Extract From the Minutes of the
                        Session of July 17, 1919</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Exchange of Goods Between the
                        Countries of Central Europe</hi></p>
                <p>The Council notes a telegram from the Allied Missions of Railways and of Supply
                    at Warsaw, dated July 13 (doc. 248) on the subject of reestablishing and
                    regulating the exchange of goods, such as potatoes and coal, between Poland on
                    one side and Germany, German Austria, and Czecho-Slovakia on the other.</p>
                <p>It has been decided: <list>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                        <item>To submit for the approval of the Supreme Council the proposals made
                            by the Allied Missions of Railways and of Supply.</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                        <item>To leave full liberty to the Italian Government to name, if it so
                            desires, a representative on the committees which will be formed at
                            points of transit with the object of supervising the execution of the
                            regulations governing traffic.</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
